course: dictionary
lesson: 4632
title: Himalayan: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Himalayan usually tells you that something is to do with the Himalayas, a huge range of mountains in Asia that includes Mount Everest. «The Himalayan mountains were covered in snow.» The clue is in the word mountains: Himalayan says where they are.
explain: The same word can also name a thing, so read the words around it. «My Himalayan curled up on the sofa» is about a cat, because curling up on a sofa is something a pet does. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a place, an animal or a kind of salt?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Himalayan salt» means pinkish rock salt mined in Pakistan. Mined means dug out of the ground, which is the clue that it is a rock, not sea water. When the clues are not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: Himalayan describes things to do with the Himalayas, a mountain range in Asia.
fact: The Himalayas include Mount Everest, the highest mountain in the world.
fact: A Himalayan can also be a long-haired cat with markings like a Siamese.
fact: Himalayan salt is pinkish rock salt mined in Pakistan.
fact: Himalayan balsam is a weed whose seed pods burst open on hot, dry days, flinging out its seeds.
exercise: «The Himalayan jumping spider lives over six thousand metres above sea level.» What does Himalayan describe here? | *The Himalayas, a mountain range in Asia | A desert in Africa | A breed of cat | A kind of rock salt
exercise: Sam says, «My Himalayan sleeps on the warm radiator.» What is a Himalayan here? | A desert in Africa | A weed with seed pods | A pinkish rock salt | *A long-haired cat with markings like a Siamese
exercise: «Himalayan salt» is used on the dinner table. What is it? | Sugar from a mountain | A breed of dog | Salt from the sea, collected on a beach | *Pinkish rock salt mined in Pakistan
test: In the Magician's sentence, «Elephant, North, the Himalayan Mountains», which direction goes with the Himalayan Mountains? | East | *North | South | West
test: «Himalayan balsam has pods that dry and twist on hot dry days until they burst.» What happens to the pods? | They glow in the dark | They turn into rock salt | They float down the river | *They burst open and fling the seeds out
exam: Which sentence uses Himalayan to mean a cat? | «Himalayan salt was sprinkled on the chips.» | «Himalayan balsam grew beside the river.» | «The Himalayan mountains were white with snow.» | *«My Himalayan curled up on the sofa.»
